of any sequence or potential meld, minimizing the risk of others claiming it while preserving flexibility for forming pungs or kongs in other suits.  \nReason: T8 is a single terminal tile with limited utility in current hand structure. Discarding it maintains focus on higher-value suited tiles (W3, W6, B2-B4) for pung/kong opportunities, aligns with concealed hand strategy, and avoids giving opponents a chance to complete chows.  \nAnswer: Play T8"}
