eed to look for chows or other patterns.\n\nLooking at the suited tiles:\n\nCharacters: W1, W3, W3, W6, W6. Maybe there's a way to form chows here. For example, if I have W1, W3, maybe I need a W2 to make a chow of 1-2-3. But I don't have W2. Alternatively, W3 and W6 could be part of a chow if I have consecutive numbers. But I have two W3s and two W6s. Not sure.\n\nBamboos: T3, T4. If I get a T5, that would make a chow. But I don't have it now.\n\nDots: B2, B3, B4. That's a sequence! B2, B3, B4 can form a chow. So that's a possible chow. Then I have B7 and B8, which could be part of another chow if I have B9. But I don't have B9. So maybe B2-B3-B4 is a chow. Then B7-B8 could be part of a chow if I have B9, but I don't. So maybe that's a two-tile sequence.\n\nHonors: F2 and F3. Not much there unless I get another F2 or F3 for a pair or a Pung.\n\nSo maybe my current hand has some chows and pairs. Let's see:\n\nIf I can form B2-B3-B4 as a chow, that's three tiles. Then maybe W3-W3 could be a pair. Then W6-W6 as another pair. Then W1 as a single. But that's not enough. Wait, I have 13 tiles. Let me try to break it down.\n\nPossible melds:\n\n- B2-B3-B4 (chow)\n- W3-W3 (pair)\n- W6-W6 (pair)\n- W1 (single)\n- T3-T4 (single)\n- F2-F3 (single)\n\nThat's not a valid hand. Need four melds and a pair. So maybe I need to adjust.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can form a chow of W3-W4-W5, but I don't have those. Or W6-W7-W8, but I don't have W7 or W8. So not helpful.\n\nLooking at the Dots again: B2, B3, B4 can form a chow. Then B7 and B8 could be part of a chow if I have B9. But I don't. So maybe B7-B8 is a pair? If I discard B7 or B8, maybe I can form a pair. But I only have one of each. So that's not possible.\n\nLooking at the Bamboos: T3 and T4. If I can get T5, that's a chow. But I don't have it. Alternatively, maybe there's a way to form a pair with T3 or T4. But I only have one of each.\n\nHonors: F2 and F3. If I can get another F2 or F3, that would make a pair. But I have 